==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilegeEnforced  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_LeastPrivilegeEnforced.als
    rationale: Removing the enforcement that successful operations require an allowed role lets the model construct a Success operation whose caller's role set has no cell in the permission matrix for the op kind (e.g., an auditor-only user successfully POSTing).
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_005_AuditorReadOnly
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_005_AuditorReadOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequiredBeforeBusinessLogic  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AuthRequiredBeforeBusinessLogic.als
    rationale: Removing the auth-before-business-logic fact lets the model invent an unauthenticated operation that nonetheless succeeds, which AuthRequiredEverywhere is meant to catch.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompletenessForTransitions  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AuditCompletenessForTransitions.als
    rationale: Removing the audit-completeness fact allows a successful state-changing operation to exist without a paired audit entry, which AuditCompleteness must flag.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Without the append-only fact, two distinct audit entries can record the same transition on the same application, which is exactly the duplication AppendOnly forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoSelfAssignment  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_NoSelfAssignment.als
    rationale: Removing no-self-assignment lets an application be assigned to its own applicant; combined with the assigned-officer-patches rule, this yields a successful PATCH where caller == applicant, violating no-self-mutation.
    expected to FAIL: NoSelfMutation, FR_011_NoSelfAssignment, FR_013_NoSelfDecision
      - NoSelfMutation: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NoSelfAssignment: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_NoSelfDecision: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoInformationLeakageOnRead  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_NoInformationLeakageOnRead.als
    rationale: Removing the not-found-on-denial fact lets the model expose a Forbidden outcome for an authenticated GET denial, which leaks resource existence and is exactly what NoInformationLeakage forbids.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_020_ByteEquivalent
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_020_ByteEquivalent: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedReadAccess  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedReadAccess.als
    rationale: Removing ownership-gated read access lets a stranger (not applicant, not assigned officer, not auditor) successfully GET an application, which OwnershipBasedAccess must catch.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)

